"'''Night Fever'''" is a song written and performed by the [[Bee Gees]]. It first appeared on [[Saturday Night Fever (soundtrack)|the soundtrack]] to ''[[Saturday Night Fever]]'' on [[RSO Records]]. The song bounded up the [[Billboard (magazine)|''Billboard'']] charts while the Bee Gees’ two previous hits from ''Saturday Night Fever'' soundtrack ("[[How Deep Is Your Love (Bee Gees song)|How Deep Is Your Love]]" and "[[Stayin' Alive]]") were still in the top ten.

The record debuted on the [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]] Chart at #76, then leaped up 44 positions to #32. It then moved: 32–17–8–5–2–1. It remained at #1 for eight weeks (the most for any single that year), and ultimately spent 13 weeks in the top 10.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.racpro.com/grid.php?pid=4&sid=1770&type=ht|title=Song-Database "Night Fever"|date=2018-07-02|website=song-database.com/|access-date=2018-07-02}}</ref> For the first five weeks that "Night Fever" was at #1, "Stayin' Alive" was at #2. Also, for one week in March, songs written by Barry Gibb held five of the top ten positions on the Hot 100 chart, and four of the top five positions, with "Night Fever" at the top of the list.<ref>{{Cite web|url=http://www.columbia.edu/~brennan/beegees/78.html|title=Gibb Songs : 1978|website=www.columbia.edu|access-date=2018-07-04}}</ref> The B-side of "Night Fever" is a live version of "Down the Road" taken from the Bee Gees' 1977 album, ''[[Here at Last... Bee Gees... Live]]''.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.allmusic.com/album/here-at-lastbee-geeslive-mw0000207268|title=Here at Last...Bee Gees...Live |website=[[AllMusic]]|access-date=2018-07-04}}</ref>

